# Everything a harness run produces.
#
# A scenario is its inputs: INTENT.md, openexec.yaml, the source tree and the
# tests that judge the outcome. Everything else under a scenario directory is
# what one run on one machine happened to do — and run-harness.sh proves it, by
# starting each scenario with `rm -rf .openexec` and building the state again
# from scratch. Committing it meant every run produced a dirty tree that could
# only be discarded.
scenarios/*/.openexec/
scenarios/*/claude-*.log

# The harness registers itself with OpenExec when run from the repository root.
.openexec/
